A||||45||3.8T Fiero GT||What's this "NO GOOD AT HIGH SPEEDS" thing I hear about from 'vette owners?||||1||
Z||000000||3.8T Fiero GT||12-02-2001||03:51 AM||||After reading the 'vette "Fiero bashing <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">" thread i wondered about something can u guys expands? advise?<P>I know we have to watch out for "bump steer" and all, but whats this about the Fiero being unstable at high speeds??? This is the first i hear of such a statement?? I will have finished my Fiero (which SHOULD) be fast over the winter...and I was plannig some nice highway runs, but now they got me thinking???  at 150 mph one vette guy said.....thats about 220+ km/h right?? ****  my done up civic did that no prob and felt safe...<P>I thought Fiero aerodynamics were good, as the handling is too?  It wont lift of the ground or feel unstable will it? I will not have a spoiler either...<P>------------------<BR>*Your ASS here*   <IMG SRC="http://www.plaudersmilies.de/rough/zzwhip.gif"> <BR><B>"A 3.8T makes and excellent "RICE" cooker"</B>||||reg||1
Z||000001||California Kid||12-02-2001||04:28 AM||||Real High Speed requires the front aero nose and the front end should be dropped an inch and a half to two inches below stock height. The headlamp doors will blow open at about 105 to 110mph, you want this to happen as pressure is building behind the facia. lifting the front end. Trick is to wire the doors so they'll only open about 1 inch. If you really want to be "trick" rig of some hidden vents to let the air pressure out into the wheel well or reverse NASA scoop on each facia side.<P>The Rear Wing will give some benefit by keeping the tail end of the car from rising at these high speeds (I'm talking above 140mph). Some years back my car was up to 165mph out in the old west desert area, very stable and glued to the road.<P>By all means do not attempt to push the car to these limits until everything is perfect on the car, I mean everything!! And you better be 50 miles from nowhere when you attempt to push these limits, I mean nothing around, not even trees.  Don't forget to check the speed rating on your tires!!!!<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/californiakidsig_2.gif"> <p>[This message has been edited by California Kid (edited 12-02-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||BlackStang95||12-02-2001||04:36 AM||||Nothing is really "good" or safe at the speeds you're talking.  Like cally said just make sure everythings cool and go for it, I've done 125 in my stock stang and things still felt fine.  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||stimpy||12-02-2001||04:39 AM||||My GT is at stock ride height. I start loosing my nerve around 115. Combination of front end lift and fear of tickets. But mostly fear of tickets.||||reg||1
Z||000004||LoW_KeY||12-02-2001||09:46 AM||||Oooh yeah fear of tickets is my biggest problem  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>AIM: FierFormula88   <P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/kcbanner.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||yo_sweet||12-02-2001||11:59 AM||||I did about 120mph down the 407 with 4 bald tires and a passenger  the car hel no prob..<P>i ahve an 86 se<P>------------------<BR>1986 Fiero SE 2.8lv6<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/dance.gif">  <P><BR>www.geocities.com/acme_s2000/intro.html<BR>yo_sweet!||||reg||1
Z||000006||VeeSixGeeTee||12-02-2001||12:27 PM||||I back off around like 115 usually..that is really fast..wouldn't want to hit a tree.  But I try really hard not to beat my car or abuse it..that girl is getting old  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Mikey<BR>85 GT 4sp..Taking a six month nap!<BR>AIM: KilleredGT||||reg||1
Z||000007||Slammed Fiero||12-02-2001||12:33 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 3.8T Fiero GT:<BR><B>After reading the 'vette "Fiero bashing  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">" thread i wondered about something can u guys expands? advise?<P>I know we have to watch out for "bump steer" and all, but whats this about the Fiero being unstable at high speeds??? This is the first i hear of such a statement?? I will have finished my Fiero (which SHOULD) be fast over the winter...and I was plannig some nice highway runs, but now they got me thinking???  at 150 mph one vette guy said.....thats about 220+ km/h right?? ****  my done up civic did that no prob and felt safe...<P>I thought Fiero aerodynamics were good, as the handling is too?  It wont lift of the ground or feel unstable will it? I will not have a spoiler either...<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Optimistic speedo in the civic??? Sport compact car did a test to see how fast they could get a civic to go , with a supercharger it would only pull off 132mph.<P>The lower your fiero the better it will feel at high speeds , 220Km/h is 140mph.(approx)<P>No car is "safe" at tripple digit speeds , safety depends on the driver. I have had my car to 5600rpm in 4th (4spd car) or about 136mph with tire correction. Rock solid. A vette does feel more planted at those speeds I can speak from experience. at 135mph it's smooth as silk.<P>JM <P><P>------------------<BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals, Big Bore TB, 70Hp Shot of NOS Autocrossed , Tracked , Dragged? (soon) abused.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Mach10||12-02-2001||01:49 PM||||Short wheel base == less high-speed stability. It's the trade off you get when a car is built for handling, rather than flat-out speed. That's why lambos and the upper-end Ferraris are so long.<P>||||reg||6
Z||000009||Tabs31||12-02-2001||01:54 PM||||I went full speed with my iron duke and it ran and sounded great. I love running my fiero at full speed. But only on the highway <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tabs31_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||Formula88||12-02-2001||02:22 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by yo_sweet:<BR><B>I did about 120mph down the 407 with 4 bald tires and a passenger  the car hel no prob..<P>i ahve an 86 se<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well, that was stupid.  Driving on bald tires is dangerous enough, but doing high speed on bald tires is just plain moronic.  Do you <I>want</I> to die, or do you just think you're immortal?<P>Sorry if I'm busting your chops here, but I've seen the aftermath of what can happen.  Buddy of mine in High School took his '79 Trans Am for a high speed run.  Yup, he had bald tires.  He left the road at about 110mph and hit a tree (5' off the ground).  The steering wheel was pushed into the back seat - so no, he didn't survive.  His car was in perfect condition, and he was an excellent driver.  But, being a broke H.S. student, he didn't bother getting new tires when he should have - and trying to show off cost him his life.<P>Also, I'm all for personal responsibility.  If you want to do something stupid and it costs you your life - go ahead.  But you do it on public streets and have a passenger in the car, you're risking their life too.  Remind me to stay the hell away from you 'till you grow out of your little "show off" phase (assuming you live that long).||||reg||13
Z||000011||Devotshka||12-02-2001||02:44 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Slammed Fiero:<BR><B>  Sport compact car did a test to see how fast they could get a civic to go , with a supercharger it would only pull off 132mph.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hehe!  I remember that one... I believe they eloquently described the problem as an "aerodynamic brick wall"   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000012||3.8T Fiero GT||12-02-2001||03:15 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Slammed Fiero:<BR><B> Optimistic speedo in the civic??? Sport compact car did a test to see how fast they could get a civic to go , with a supercharger it would only pull off 132mph.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>My engine was from Japan (1991) excellent condition, DOHC 16V, non vtec....140 HP stock with intake, header exhaust, NEW z-rated tires and ground effects on a little 88.  IT DID 220km/h  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  u dont have to beleive me if u dont want too.  the motor was excellent!<P>The motor/setup u are thinking of is a little 127 hp SOHC motor with jackson racing SC probably, on an Si version (or EX in the US), those SOHC are nothing compard to japans DOHC motors.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000013||Jaei Sun||12-02-2001||03:16 PM||||I've been up to 155 in a fiero.<P>Jimmy's V8 Fiero the speedo was str8 down.  So he figured out from the RPMs of the engine and tire size that we were in the ball park of 150-160 MPH.  And it felt stable to me.||||reg||1
Z||000014||BlackStang95||12-02-2001||03:46 PM||||the one in the article had a supercharger, so didn't it have to be making more than your non vtec engine regardless?||||reg||1
Z||000015||Standard||12-02-2001||04:07 PM||||I had my quad up to around 120 for a little bit.  Felt pretty solid, but it's also dropped 2 inches.  Headlight doors stayed shut, too.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_pic_full.jpg">          <BR><FONT COLOR="red">1988 Quad 4 Coupe 5 speed</FONT><BR><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="white">1986 GT 5 speed, 1984 SC Auto</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="blue">AOL: LastMinuteBastrd  AIM: SavedbyJebus</FONT></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000016||Mach10||12-02-2001||04:42 PM||||All the power in the WORLD won't raise your top speed when you run out of gears :wathcout:||||reg||12
Z||000017||rogergarrison||12-02-2001||04:49 PM||||as you see, i have a Ferrari 308 style kit on my 86SE. it does get a little lite feeling in the nose over 125 or so, but above 140 the shape of the nose,hood, and fenders starts generating more downforce so it gets more stable going faster, Iv had it to around 175. I just recently got an 88 Vette, and its all tite in suspension but it has wicked bump steer at speed. I feel thats due to tire size and the car being so heavy. I feel much safer and stable at high speed in my Fiero. But again remember my body is quite a bit different aerodynamicly.My Fiero has completely stock suspension other than Bilstien struts and shocks.<P>------------------<BR>           <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/rogergarrison1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000018||avengador1||12-02-2001||06:30 PM||||From my younger foolish days, I can say that driving at those speeds is nuts and requires 100% of your concentration. Also at 140 MPH the white strips start to look like a solid line and two lanes look like one. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_dizzy.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000019||rx7speed||12-02-2001||08:26 PM||||had my rx7 up to 145 before I put the turbo on<P><BR>was still pulling though but I was on a bumpy road and saw a car comming so I had to shut her down<BR>and yes my nerve was kinda leaving me also<P>stock susp with mostly stock motor<P>car did just fine though||||reg||1
Z||000020||Tina||12-02-2001||09:12 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 3.8T Fiero GT:<BR><B>I thought Fiero aerodynamics were good, as the handling is too?  It wont lift of the ground or feel unstable will it? I will not have a spoiler either...<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>No complaints here anymore, although not in the habit of driving around doing those speeds for a long time(just short bursts).<BR>I could definitly tell the difference between<BR>the 84 last year<BR>(stock height, aging suspension, no hood vent)<BR>Started to feel a bit floaty in the front end over est. 120mph<BR>To my 84 lookalike this year<BR>(2 inch lower, totally redone suspension and hood vent)<BR>Firmly planted at 120mph and above.<P>Tina  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>BTW Spoiler added last month didn't seem to make a difference.<BR>But perhaps it being higher than stock, or me just plain not noticing the difference.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000021||Ayrow||12-02-2001||10:33 PM||||While driving through a very sparse area of New Mexico, I had my '88 Formula up to 140mph several times (at least that's what the speedo said).<P>California Kid is right, the headlight doors would flip open at that speed.<P>Other than that, the car was pretty stable for the most part..<P>Ayrow<P>||||reg||1
Z||000022||California Kid||12-02-2001||10:52 PM||||Just a little side note about the headlamp doors and high speed (assuming they are closed). If you don't do a modification to prevent them from flipping open, they will beat them selves to dead, breaking the assembly.||||reg||1
Z||000023||AgaricX||12-02-2001||10:57 PM||||I have Tom's headlight kit installed on mine.  I'm soon to put lexan covers on them... Is this bad for the aerodynamic stability at +100mph?  If so, what should I do to help?  what sort of vent needs to be installed in the hood to help?<P>In my old Z I could do 130 on straightaways with no problem.  I havent taken my Fiero that high yet.<P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.agaric.net/fiero/AgaricX.jpg">  <BR>'85 SE 3800SC 5 Spd<BR>I WANT A FASTBACK!!!||||reg||1
Z||000024||3.8T Fiero GT||12-02-2001||11:39 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by California Kid:<BR><B>Just a little side note about the headlamp doors and high speed (assuming they are closed). If you don't do a modification to prevent them from flipping open, they will beat them selves to dead, breaking the assembly.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>well should i be worried about them like flying off or causing a break in the airflow slowing the car or making it unstable??<P>couldnt i just pop them up while doing that speed eventhough i know it will hurt the airflow a bit. and what about running outta gears?? will it happen??????<P>well guess i will let u guys know what happens   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  duct tape it is!!!!!!!!! the solution to all car problems!!!!!!!!!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>*Your ASS here*    <IMG SRC="http://www.plaudersmilies.de/rough/zzwhip.gif">  <BR><B>"A 3.8T makes and excellent "RICE" cooker"</B><p>[This message has been edited by 3.8T Fiero GT (edited 12-02-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000025||California Kid||12-03-2001||12:41 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by AgaricX:<BR><B>I have Tom's headlight kit installed on mine.  I'm soon to put lexan covers on them... Is this bad for the aerodynamic stability at +100mph?  If so, what should I do to help?  what sort of vent needs to be installed in the hood to help?<BR>In my old Z I could do 130 on straightaways with no problem.  I havent taken my Fiero that high yet.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>********************************************<BR>With the flush mount lamps and covers you are going to build pressure in the front end, in other words the front will get very light. I see 3 choices, hood vent (reverse), ducts to wheel houses, or reverse NASA duct on the side lower facia. All treatments should be a flush as possible without increasing exposed frontal surface area. Do a search on what I think is called the Daber Hood, it will scavenge air from the facia cavity and improve flow through the radiator.<BR>Picture of LT1 Chop Top added to show hood.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ChopTopFiero3_1.jpg"> <p>[This message has been edited by California Kid (edited 12-03-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000026||NOCONES||12-03-2001||12:49 AM||||Roger? what engine trans mods have you done to a fiero to make it go 175??  i just don't think with a fiero tranny the gearing is there? or is it? just wondering.<BR><P>------------------<BR>NOCONES<BR>-84 2M4 <BR>-4.10 4-speed<BR>-SCCA sollo II <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Nocones_1.jpg"> <P>Addmit it... it's just as much fun alone...  Solo II||||reg||1
Z||000027||rmorgandotcom||12-03-2001||01:06 AM||||Hey ayrow, thats pretty much all of the state!  I know a good spot but there are MPs around there.||||reg||1
Z||000028||California Kid||12-03-2001||01:08 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 3.8T Fiero GT:<BR><B>  well should i be worried about them like flying off or causing a break in the airflow slowing the car or making it unstable??<BR>couldnt i just pop them up while doing that speed eventhough i know it will hurt the airflow a bit. and what about running outta gears?? will it happen??????<BR>well guess i will let u guys know what happens    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  duct tape it is!!!!!!!!! the solution to all car problems!!!!!!!!!!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>********************************************<BR>Headlamp up or doors flopping up and down will be like air brakes reducing your attainable top speed, pretty significant.<P>If you duct tape them shut you're going to build pressure causing very light steering, you'll feel it, it's no surprise unless you encounter a sharp turn for the speed you're going.<P>You really don't run out of gears, you either max your tach out, or there is so much air resistance the car just doesn't want to go any faster. Typical problem with some 6 spd trans is that the car will have a higher top end in 5th instead of 6th gear. Horsepower and Torque v/s aerodynamic drag.<P>Anyway it's late, going to bed, tried to explain this briefly, hope it helps.<P>Just want to remind you this is risky business, better have your act together, it's not like something going wrong at 45mph!!! I'm only adding comments because if you really want to go that fast, you're going to do it anyway, just try to be as smart as you can. Too many people have died because they didn't have it figured out.||||reg||1
Z||000029||fieroX||12-03-2001||01:15 AM||||two words, hood vents<P> <IMG SRC="http://home.kscable.com/ccheney/ryanpict/paragonvents1.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fierox.com/logo2small.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000030||rogergarrison||12-03-2001||06:35 AM||||I have taller tires to fill wheel wells and it does change final ratio. Also have modified 3.1, FI, with IRM turbo. Redline is 7500 rpm, dyno hp when I built it was around 275. I have homemade flush headlites with lexan covers and no hood or fender vents. The headlite covers are just velcroed on and I havent had one come off yet, so I dont know about the air pressure blowing them open. I never had a prob with the original pop ups coming open either. I guess depends on how hard your springs are. ps=I raced stock cars years ago, so Im comfortable at those speeds as long as there is no other traffic around, and no distractions like radios. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>            <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/rogergarrison1.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 12-03-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000031||Formula||12-03-2001||07:17 AM||||the autos top speed is limited by the 3rd gear. a stock 2.8 will easily pull all the way through it to redline.||||reg||1
Z||000032||falconhulk||12-03-2001||08:10 AM||||Bald tires would theoretically be better for high speed runs.  Remember thatslicks are "Bald".  ||||reg||1
Z||000033||Wannabe||12-03-2001||09:30 AM||||Common misunderstanding. The usable rubber on a street tire is in the treads. When they are gone, the rubber underneath will not give good traction. Besides, the fact that the tires have been in service long enough that the tread is gone means they are long past any kind of ideal condition. Simply put, don't drive on bald tires.||||reg||1
Z||000034||Patrick's Dad||12-03-2001||10:31 AM||||&lt;quote&gt;Hehe! I remember that one... I believe they eloquently described the problem as an "aerodynamic brick wall"&lt;/quote&gt;<P>I drove one of those; our old 1992 Ford Exploder! Couldn't go any faster than 85mph.<P>I seem to remember a thread a while back that referred to the "erie calm" of a Fiero in triple digits. That, plus fear of citations, has limited me to the 110mph bracket in my mostly stock Formula.||||reg||10
