Z||000038||Gerald||12-03-2001||07:02 PM||||Before my fear of winter and tickets I got my 87 coupe (duke) to 115 mph. My covers didnt come up. But one time I was going about 105 mph and a truck went by me. then the covers flew up. Scared the hell outta me. I thought someone was shooting at me. lol<BR>As for fear of tickets I got to go to court tomorow.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Gerald (edited 12-03-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000039||artherd||12-03-2001||07:04 PM||||Unstable?  Nooooo.....<P>My t-top car feels *more* stable at 130 than it does at 80. (17s, new suspension bushings and wearables all around, including steering rack, etc.) That's it....<P>The aerodynamics of the front however DO need to be fixed though to drive the car at speed, Two words: Hood Vents! (easiest, though there are other ways.)<P>PS: Only test this on sanctioned private race tracks, never on public roads  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Best!<BR>Ben<P><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000040||fieroX||12-04-2001||02:13 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by artherd:<BR><B> Two words: Hood Vents! <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Do I hear an echo in here?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>||||reg||1
