Z||000042||California Kid||12-04-2001||09:17 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by lowCG:<BR><B>I have a huge vent in my hood,and the headlight doors still come open at higher speeds.<BR>I'd like to try the idea of venting air through the wheel-arches.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Have you got any pictures of your hood? I'd be curious to see what your arrangement is, don't understand why your still building pressure (it may be that at that speed you just can't flow enought air through the Radiator core to make enough difference)?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000043||artherd||12-05-2001||04:16 AM||||Um, you ARE venting out of the open part of the hood, right?  Not the spare tire compartment?<P>Even withought hood vents, both my Formulas wouldn't lift the headlights at 130 (and neither car would go any faster  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by lowCG:<BR><B>I have a huge vent in my hood,and the headlight doors still come open at higher speeds.<BR>I'd like to try the idea of venting air through the wheel-arches.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000044||Philphine||12-05-2001||07:28 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Patrick's Dad:<P>I seem to remember a thread a while back that referred to the "erie calm" of a Fiero in triple digits. That, plus fear of citations, has limited me to the 110mph bracket in my mostly stock Formula.[/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>i remember that line i think. it was part of an article for the indy pace car (an '84 motor trend article i think) which they described as being near stock suspension wise.<P>a little nose rubbing ammo. the article said it had the highest top speed up to that time of any prior pace car. that would include '78.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000045||California Kid||12-05-2001||09:47 AM||||Ben makes a very good point about the Formula's, the nose is a different design than the GT's I was referring to. If you compare the GT to the Formula and other models you'll see the GT Front Fascia has larger air inlet square inch area at the turn signals and radiator air intake.<P>Consider GT Facia modification of "flush" clear lens at turn signal pockets, or flush signal lens lamps relocated on facia. Modify current lamp pocket with dryer duct hose to cool brakes (air directed into wheel house).<P>To each his own!!! I think West Coast Fiero even sells a wires strap kit for the headlamp doors (not expensive) to prevent this from happening, but it's doesn't address the air pressure issue.||||reg||1
